<details><summary>Solution</summary>First, by Vietas Formulas, we can determine that \begin{align*}\alpha_1+\alpha_2+\alpha_3+\alpha_4&=-2,\alpha_1\alpha_2+\alpha_1\alpha_3+\alpha_1\alpha_4+\alpha_2\alpha_3+\alpha_2\alpha_4+\alpha_3\alpha_4&=0,\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_3+\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_4+\alpha_1\alpha_3\alpha_4+\alpha_2\alpha_3\alpha_4&=0,\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_3\alpha_4&=2.\end{align*}
Let  $X=\alpha_1\alpha_2+\alpha_3\alpha_4$ ,  $Y=\alpha_1\alpha_3+\alpha_2\alpha_4$ ,  $Z=\alpha_1\alpha_4+\alpha_2\alpha_3$ .  We first see that  $X+Y+Z=0$ .  Next, we try to evaluate  $XY+XZ+YZ$ .  By substituting out our expressions for  $X$ ,  $Y$ , and  $Z$ , expanding the expression, and simplifying, we get that \begin{align*}&(\alpha_1\alpha_2+\alpha_3\alpha_4)(\alpha_1\alpha_3+\alpha_2\alpha_4)+(\alpha_1\alpha_2+\alpha_3\alpha_4)(\alpha_1\alpha_4+\alpha_2\alpha_3)+(\alpha_1\alpha_3+\alpha_2\alpha_4)(\alpha_1\alpha_4+\alpha_2\alpha_3)&=\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_3(\alpha_1+\alpha_2+\alpha_3)+\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_4(\alpha_1+\alpha_2+\alpha_4)+\alpha_1\alpha_3\alpha_4(\alpha_1+\alpha_3+\alpha_4)+\alpha_2\alpha_3\alpha_4(\alpha_2+\alpha_3+\alpha_4)&=\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_3(-2-\alpha_4)+\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_4(-2-\alpha_3)+\alpha_1\alpha_3\alpha_4(-2-\alpha_2)+\alpha_2\alpha_3\alpha_4(-2-\alpha_1)&=-2(\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_3+\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_4+\alpha_1\alpha_3\alpha_4+\alpha_2\alpha_3\alpha_4)-4\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_3\alpha_4&=-2(0)-4(2)&=-8\end{align*}  Therefore we have  $XY+XZ+YZ=-8$ .

Now we get to work on  $XYZ$ .

\begin{align*}&(\alpha_1\alpha_2+\alpha_3\alpha_4)(\alpha_1\alpha_3+\alpha_2\alpha_4)(\alpha_1\alpha_4+\alpha_2\alpha_3)&=\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_3\alpha_4(\alpha_1^2+\alpha_2^2+\alpha_3^2+\alpha_4^2)+\left[(\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_3)^2+(\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_4)^2+(\alpha_1\alpha_3\alpha_4)^2+(\alpha_2\alpha_3\alpha_4)^2\right].\end{align*}

This expression consists of two simpler expressions, which we can evaluate separately.  First, we see that \begin{align*}&\alpha_1^2+\alpha_2^2+\alpha_3^2+\alpha_4^2&=(\alpha_1+\alpha_2+\alpha_3+\alpha_4)^2-2(\alpha_1\alpha_2+\alpha_1\alpha_3+\alpha_1\alpha_4+\alpha_2\alpha_3+\alpha_2\alpha_4+\alpha_3\alpha_4)&=(-2)^2-2(0)&=4\end{align*} This means that  $\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_3\alpha_4(\alpha_1^2+\alpha_2^2+\alpha_3^2+\alpha_4^2)=(-2)(4)=-8$ .

Next, we see that
\begin{align*}&(\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_3)^2+(\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_4)^2+(\alpha_1\alpha_3\alpha_4)^2+(\alpha_2\alpha_3\alpha_4)^2&=(\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_3+\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_4+\alpha_1\alpha_3\alpha_4+\alpha_2\alpha_3\alpha_4)^2-\alpha_1\alpha_2\alpha_3\alpha_4(\alpha_1\alpha_2+\alpha_1\alpha_3+\alpha_1\alpha_4+\alpha_2\alpha_3+\alpha_2\alpha_4+\alpha_3\alpha_4)&=0^2-2(0)&=0.\end{align*}

Finally, we have that  $XYZ=-8+0=-8$ .

Now we have the system of equations \[\begin{cases}X+Y+Z=0XY+XZ+YZ=-8XYZ=-8\end{cases}\] which means  $X$ ,  $Y$ , and  $Z$  are the roots of the equation  $t^3-8t-8=0$ .  By plugging in small values of  $t$ , we see that  $t=-2$  is a root, so by performing the synthetic division we get that  $(t+2)(t^2-2t-4)=0$ .  Solving the second quadratic for  $t$  gives us the unordered set  $\boxed{\left\{-2,1+\sqrt{5},1-\sqrt{5}\right\}}$  as our final answer.</details>

