&= \frac{5603x^2}{3} 
x^2 &= \frac{7^2\cdot 20^2\cdot 3}{5603} 
x &= \frac{7\cdot 20\sqrt{3}}{\sqrt{5603}}
\end{align*}

Now, we find the areas.  $\sin\angle BCD = \sin(2\theta) = 2\sin\theta\cos\theta = 2\cdot\frac{10\sqrt{341}}{21^2}$ ,
so  $[BCD] = \frac12\cdot 3\cdot 4\cdot 2\cdot\frac{10\sqrt{341}}{21^2} = \frac{40\sqrt{341}}{147}$ .
