void arr(picture p, pair A, pair B) {
 	draw(p, (t * A + (1-t) * B)--(t * B + (1-t) * A), Arrow(TeXHead));
}

picture p1, p2;
dot(p1, " $3$ ", (-1,4), N);
dot(p1, " $4$ ", (-2,4), N);
dot(p1, " $5$ ", (1,4), N);
dot(p1, " $6$ ", (1,2), E);
dot(p1, " $1$ ", (0,2), N);
dot(p1, " $2$ ", (-1,2), W);
dot(p1, " $7$ ", (0,0), S);
arr(p1, (-2, 4), (-1, 2)); 
arr(p1, (-1, 4), (-1, 2)); 
arr(p1, (1, 4), (1, 2)); 
arr(p1, (-1, 2), (0, 0)); 
arr(p1, (0, 2), (0, 0)); 
arr(p1, (1, 2), (0, 0)); 

add(p1);

dot(p2, " $3$ ", (-1,4), N);
dot(p2, " $4$ ", (-2,4), N);
dot(p2, " $5$ ", (2,2), N);
dot(p2, " $6$ ", (2,0), E);
dot(p2, " $1$ ", (0,2), N);
dot(p2, " $2$ ", (-1,2), W);
dot(p2, " $7$ ", (0,0), S);
arr(p2, (-2, 4), (-1, 2)); 
arr(p2, (-1, 4), (-1, 2)); 
arr(p2, (-1, 2), (0, 0)); 
arr(p2, (0, 2), (0, 0)); 
arr(p2, (2, 2), (2, 0)); 
arr(p2, (2, 0), (0, 0)); 
arr(p2, (0, 0), (2, 0)); 

label(" $\longleftrightarrow$ ", (3, 2));

add(shift((6, 0))*p2);
[/asy]
(Self loop on  $7$  not shown.  $6$  is pulled down/pushed up).**Claim 2:**  $C_1'(x) = A(x)$ .
*Proof:* The  $*$  label corresponds to  $n+1$ , so it must be at the root, so we can cut down the arborescence into a bunch of subarborescences that satisfy the label restriction, so are almost elements of  $C_1$ , except the roots do not have self loops. For each subarborescence, if the root has the max label, just add a self loop to it; these are in bijection with  $C_1$ . Otherwise, pull down the max label vertex from the first level above the root to biject with elements of  $C_2$ . The inverse is clear (push up the max labeled vertex of those in  $C_2$ , connect into arborescence).
[asy]
